{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on the DX-A2 contract questions (request 1c124ebf, reads that wait for a head), answering c76d957f. Order unchanged: 121a8913, 7c0e8181, J4, then DX-A2 in its slot.\n\n1. Form. `atLeast: number | FactRef`. A number asks for a position in the scope the read already names. A FactRef asks for that position in that scope and incarnation; a FactRef for another scope or incarnation answers `wrong-incarnation` at once. Receipt-aware reads forward the receipt's fact unchanged.\n\n2. What the wait proves. Only that the scope's head is at or past the minimum, in the same scope and incarnation. The wait proves nothing about the hash at the requested position: it does not read the archive, does not restore a pruned payload, and a position below the retained floor is satisfied by any current head at or past it. `followReceipt` keeps its existing check of the returned entry's hash. No new refusal for a hash that is wrong or no longer held; that check stays where it is.\n\n3. Behind. One new refusal: `{ ok: false, reason: \"behind\", at: Head }`, with `behind` added to ReadRefusal's reasons and `at` carrying the current head. Existing failures unchanged.\n\n4. Bounds. `readWaitMilliseconds: 5000` in Bounds. At most 64 waiting reads per scope; a read past that answers `unavailable` with reason `waiters`, at once. A waiting read holds no storage transaction and releases the turn; the signed-read admission charges its one request. Authorization is rechecked before the answer is disclosed.\n\n5. Scope. The four ScopeApi reads (summary, items, history, entry) over HTTP and in-process, the client handle's reads and `followReceipt`. Generic inspect cards witness one refresh read after the act. Declared cards and applicationProjection stay out; file a one-line follow-up if the card kit needs it later. \"One request\" means one native refresh read after the accepted act, excluding authority reads before signing. \"Reads write nothing\" means no journal or domain write and no new durable wait state caused by waiting; the existing recovery scheduling of the wrappers stays as it is.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}